---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
import { ANALYTICS_ENDPOINT } from '../lib/analytics';
const analyticsOn = Boolean(ANALYTICS_ENDPOINT);
---

<Base title="Privacy policy" description="What data the Lumo app and website handle: an encrypted local database, permissions you grant, and cookieless, opt-out-respecting website analytics.">
  <PageHead eyebrow="Legal" title="Privacy policy" lede="Short version: your conversations and history are stored on your computer, Lumo only uses what you grant, and this website does not track you.">
    <p class="legal-meta">Last updated 16 October 2026 · Pre-release draft</p>
  </PageHead>
  <div class="container prose">
    <h2 id="app">The Lumo app</h2>
    <h3>What stays on your computer</h3>
    <p>
      Conversations, task history, memories, settings and the audit log are stored on your computer in an encrypted database. The database key and
      account tokens are kept in your operating system’s keychain. You choose how long history is kept, and you can delete it at any time.
    </p>
    <h3>What is sent, and to whom</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>The model provider</strong> (Anthropic) receives the messages and context needed to answer each request.</li>
      <li><strong>Web pages and search</strong> you ask Lumo to read are fetched like a browser would.</li>
      <li><strong>Services you connect</strong>, such as a calendar or GitHub, receive the requests needed for actions you ask for or approve.</li>
      <li><strong>Handoffs</strong> to delivery providers or merchants open their site in your browser; what you do there is governed by their policies.</li>
      <li><strong>Updates</strong>: the app checks for new versions, which reveals your IP address and app version to the update host.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Lumo does not include advertising, analytics or crash-reporting services in the app. Diagnostic logs stay on your computer unless you choose to share them.</p>
    <h3 id="plans">Plans and billing</h3>
    <p>
      Lumo’s plans open at launch. Before then, this policy will be updated to describe what a plan involves: any account and billing details,
      how plan limits are counted, and how requests reach the model provider.
    </p>

    <h3>Permissions</h3>
    <p>
      Folders, screen, microphone, clipboard, location and accounts are only used after you grant them, and grants can be revoked in Settings →
      Permissions. A visible indicator shows whenever the screen, microphone or input control is in use.
    </p>

    <h2 id="website">This website</h2>
    <p>This website is a set of static pages. It sets no cookies, uses no local storage for tracking, and loads no third-party scripts, fonts or embeds.</p>

    <h3 id="website-analytics">Page-view counting</h3>
    <p>
      The website includes an optional, first-party page-view counter. It is <strong>{analyticsOn ? 'currently enabled' : 'currently turned off'}</strong>:
      it is only included in the pages when the site is built with an analytics endpoint configured, and otherwise no analytics code is present at all.
    </p>
    <p>When it is enabled:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>It sends nothing if your browser has <strong>Do Not Track</strong> or <strong>Global Privacy Control</strong> turned on.</li>
      <li>Otherwise it sends one request per page view containing only: the page path, the host name of the referring site (not the full address), and a coarse screen-size class (small, medium or large).</li>
      <li>It sets no cookies, stores nothing in your browser, sends no credentials and uses no identifiers or fingerprinting, so visits cannot be linked together.</li>
      <li>The request goes to a server operated for the Lumo project, never to an advertising or analytics company.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>As with any website, the server that hosts these pages may keep standard access logs.</p>

    <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
    <p>Lumo is not directed at children under 13, and your model provider may set a higher minimum age.</p>

    <h2 id="changes">Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>
      Changes to this policy will be posted on this page with a new date. Questions can be raised as a <a href={SITE.issues}>GitHub issue</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
